--TEST--
A `LogicError` clause takes the program's own faults and nothing on the `RuntimeError` branch, counted over the whole branch rather than read off one line, and three unrelated `Core` members agree on which half their refusal belongs to — spec § 10
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: LogicError, lang:errors/the-throwable-tree
// The tree splits at the root into what the code got wrong and what the world
// said no to. What this pins is that the two halves are disjoint from both
// sides — the sweep counts, so a class that quietly grew a second parent fails
// here while every line still reads plausibly — and that the library lands its
// own refusals in the same half a program's `throw` does.

final class Halves {
    public static function raise(string $kind): void {
        if ($kind == "io") { throw new IOError("io"); }
        if ($kind == "parse") { throw new ParseError("parse"); }
        if ($kind == "timeout") { throw new TimeoutError("timeout"); }
        if ($kind == "recursion") { throw new RecursionError("recursion"); }
        throw new RuntimeError("plain");
    }

    // Every class on the other branch, asked the same question: does a
    // `LogicError` clause take it? All five must miss, and the count is what
    // asserts it — reading one arm would still pass with four of them wrong.
    public static function runtimeBranchMissed(): uint {
        array<string> $kinds = ["io", "parse", "timeout", "recursion", "plain"];
        uint $missed = 0;
        foreach ($kinds as string $kind) {
            try {
                Halves::raise($kind);
            } catch (LogicError $wrongHalf) {
            } catch (Throwable $rightHalf) {
                $missed = $missed + 1;
            }
        }
        return $missed;
    }

    // The bound from the other side: a fault the program raised itself is not
    // taken by a clause written for the world saying no, so only the root
    // admits both and neither half is a superset of the other.
    public static function ourFault(): string {
        try {
            throw new LogicError("the index was past the end");
        } catch (RuntimeError $notTheWorld) {
            return "a RuntimeError clause";
        } catch (Throwable $root) {
            return "only the root";
        }
    }

    public static function callWith(uint $which): void {
        if ($which == 0) {
            var $base = Core\BigInt::parse("101", {radix: 99});
            return;
        }
        if ($which == 1) {
            var $document = Core\Json::decode("[1]", {maxDepth: 0});
            return;
        }
        var $moved = Core\Time\Date::at(2026, 9, 19)->plus(3, Core\Unit::Hour);
    }

    // Three members with nothing in common but the judgement they make: a base
    // that does not exist, a depth outside the range, and a unit too small to
    // move a date. All three are mistakes in the call, so all three reach the
    // same clause — counted, because two agreeing and one not still prints a
    // plausible line each.
    public static function libraryAgrees(): uint {
        uint $agreed = 0;
        uint $which = 0;
        while ($which < 3) {
            try {
                Halves::callWith($which);
            } catch (LogicError $ourBug) {
                $agreed = $agreed + 1;
            } catch (Throwable $somethingElse) {
            }
            $which = $which + 1;
        }
        return $agreed;
    }

    // The name test agrees with the clause that took the value, in both
    // directions, so a program branching on `is` and a program branching on
    // `catch` cannot be told apart.
    public static function nameTest(): string {
        try {
            throw new LogicError("a state the call had no business being in");
        } catch (Throwable $caught) {
            if ($caught is RuntimeError) {
                return "and a RuntimeError";
            }
            if ($caught is LogicError) {
                return "a LogicError, not a RuntimeError";
            }
            return "neither name";
        }
    }
}

echo Halves::runtimeBranchMissed(), "\n";
echo Halves::ourFault(), "\n";
echo Halves::libraryAgrees(), "\n";
echo Halves::nameTest(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
5
only the root
3
a LogicError, not a RuntimeError
